<section class="cl1403c-a-loseground"><div class="cl1403c-a-loseground-inner"><h2>Where Interviews Break Down</h2><div class="cl1403c-a-lg-grid"><article class="cl1403c-a-lg-card"><h3>Missing the question</h3><p>Recognize what the interviewer is really asking, then choose the material that answers it.</p></article><article class="cl1403c-a-lg-card"><h3>A rigid script</h3><p>Use your own truthful experiences. Build answers that can move with a real conversation.</p></article><article class="cl1403c-a-lg-card"><h3>Unpracticed delivery</h3><p>Work on presence, pacing, voice and body language before the stakes are real.</p></article><article class="cl1403c-a-lg-card"><h3>Generic preparation</h3><p>Research programs with purpose. Connect what you learn to specific questions and better conversations.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="cl1403c-a-types" id="method"><div class="cl1403c-a-types-photo mm-alt-photo" data-bg="<?php echo $asset('media/montage-1702.webp'); ?>"><div class="cl1403c-a-types-photo-overlay"><h2>What We Train</h2><p>One connected framework. Not a collection of memorized answers.</p></div></div><div class="cl1403c-a-types-grid"><article class="cl1403c-a-type-card"><span class="cl1403c-a-type-badge">Communication</span><h3>Presence &amp; delivery</h3><p>Pacing, voice, body language and deliberate communication. Practice making your meaning clear.</p></article><article class="cl1403c-a-type-card"><span class="cl1403c-a-type-badge">Content</span><h3>Your story &amp; strategy</h3><p>Recognize the question beneath the question and choose truthful material from your experience.</p></article><article class="cl1403c-a-type-card"><span class="cl1403c-a-type-badge">Adaptability</span><h3>Formats &amp; readiness</h3><p>Traditional, behavioral, CV-based, panel and group interviews. Virtual and in-person preparation.</p></article><article class="cl1403c-a-type-card"><span class="cl1403c-a-type-badge">Connection</span><h3>Program fit &amp; follow-through</h3><p>Purposeful program research, better questions, the impression you leave and what follows.</p></article></div></section>
